/ windows: a path plang writes uses / on every OS, a user's event sees only its app's goals, and the C# suite passes
/ on Windows. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each comment a behaviour, the test under it proves it. The
/ text is start.md.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3

Stage1
/ a user's "before each goal" fires for the app's own goals only, never plang's system goals — plang test
/ /plan/windows/app/event/EachGoalIsTheAppsOwn
- call /plan/windows/app/event/EachGoalIsTheAppsOwn

Stage2
/ a path's plang form is written with / on every OS: Combine, Parent, WithExtension, Relative and a goal's .pr — C#
/ test PlangFormTests (and the Windows run)

Stage3
/ a .goal with CR LF line ends reads as its lines — C# test (the goal reader)
/ a number in text reads in the invariant culture, whatever the machine's — C# test with the culture set to is-IS
